Design-token pipeline: turn a token JSON into CSS custom properties for light and dark themes and prove contrast. /workspace/tokens: given this inline token source, write src/build.js exporting toCss(tokens) and check(tokens).

{
  "light": { "bg": "#ffffff", "surface": "#f4f4f5", "text": "#18181b", "muted": "#52525b", "accent": "#2563eb" },
  "dark":  { "bg": "#09090b", "surface": "#18181b", "text": "#fafafa", "muted": "#a1a1aa", "accent": "#60a5fa" }
}

toCss emits :root with the light set as --color-name variables and a prefers-color-scheme dark media block overriding them. check computes WCAG contrast of text and muted against bg and surface in both themes and returns failures below 4.5. Vitest: parse output with postcss asserting variable names and the media block, and assert check returns an empty failure list for this palette; add one deliberately failing palette fixture asserting it is caught. Green run.

